WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.498
Compare with what you paid.

2
00:00:01.618 --> 00:00:05.553
A price change creates a gain or loss relative to your purchase price.

3
00:00:06.083 --> 00:00:07.186
Count every share.

4
00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:13.785
Buy 2 shares at $100 and sell at $110: a $20 gain before costs.

5
00:00:14.304 --> 00:00:16.197
Use percentages to compare.

6
00:00:16.317 --> 00:00:20.160
$10 gained on a $100 share is a 10% return.

7
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.716
Percentages put different-sized trades in context.

8
00:00:24.236 --> 00:00:26.303
Realized versus unrealized.

9
00:00:26.423 --> 00:00:29.291
A result on shares you still hold is unrealized.

10
00:00:29.411 --> 00:00:31.408
Selling makes that result realized.

11
00:00:31.945 --> 00:00:33.500
Include the whole picture.

12
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.977
Fees and slippage affect real results.

13
00:00:36.097 --> 00:00:40.486
Sprout’s Profit / loss explorer lets you try hypothetical exits.

